A GnuPG-era qexo keyring, kept as a test fixture.

Generated 2026-11-14 on aletheia-core with system gpg 2.4.4,
using the exact batch spec qexo's gpg era used (eddsa /
ed25519, sign-only, %no-protection), name "qexo node
fixture", comment "qexo node key". Fingerprint:
C67424B8836BBA88E1F5B8B824570838961846C6.

This key is a public test vector. It was generated solely
for these tests, has never been a node key, is registered
nowhere, and signs nothing outside a test sandbox. Its
private half is here on purpose: the migration test needs
real GnuPG output — a fixture written by the code under
test would prove nothing.

Layout mirrors a live keyring home: pubring.kbx and
private-keys-v1.d/<keygrip>.key. trustdb.gpg and the
revocation certificate are not included; the migration
never reads them.
